## Standing sweep — does any canonical page claim a gate's build status?

A bare grep for 'accepted|implemented' is NOT evidence here: 'accepted' is core protocol
vocabulary on these pages ('an Outcome is accepted'), and such a grep returns 97 lines of
which none are status claims. The sweep below targets the failure mode instead — a gate or
packet name within 60 characters of a build-status word — and CLASSIFIES every hit rather
than printing a count. A count alone would not distinguish a pass from a broken pattern.

$ python3 statusweep.py   # regex over concepts/, mechanisms/ and the five Layer-1/2 pages
  mental-model/concepts/values.md:3  ...accepted K0.1...
  mental-model/mechanisms/actions.md:5  ...K2.3. K1 refuses Effects. This is target specification, not shipped...
  mental-model/mechanisms/authority.md:5  ...K2.2; extended by K4 and K5. This is target specification, not shipped...
